                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cfced3b3-64f3-3c5b-a761-48d6047c9f18",
                        "entry_id": "50715dae-dba3-382a-abb3-22900d3192a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "церк. рукополагать, посвящать в священный сан, совершать хиротонию"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "01bd4229-8dd4-4a53-9518-fb08ec7083c7",
                                "sense_id": "cfced3b3-64f3-3c5b-a761-48d6047c9f18",
                                "text": "14 ноября 1999 г. после пострижения в монашество в Троице-Сергиевой лавре Даниил, митрополит Токийский и всей Японии хиротонисан во епископа Киотосского, управляющего Западно-Японской епархией Японской Автономной Православной Церкви."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "05c0d223-ecc6-4a5a-b4ca-7c68ebddb104",
                        "source_entry_id": "50715dae-dba3-382a-abb3-22900d3192a0",
                        "source_sense_id": "cfced3b3-64f3-3c5b-a761-48d6047c9f18",
                        "target_lang_word": "consecrate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "consecrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5656c464-2526-3186-b588-8de5ecce0bb7",
                                        "entry_id": "90a5c753-2177-3f20-9c78-f6acb97777bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To declare something holy, or make it holy by some procedure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a656c0b-9440-4204-8ded-b3efa01f1280",
                                                "sense_id": "5656c464-2526-3186-b588-8de5ecce0bb7",
                                                "text": "But, in a larger sense, we can not dedicate—we can not consecrate—we can not hallow—this ground. The brave men, living and dead, who struggled here, have consecrated it, far above our poor power to add or detract."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8885a345-e11c-3880-8020-c9658d42ba9e",
                                        "entry_id": "90a5c753-2177-3f20-9c78-f6acb97777bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To ordain as a bishop."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "specifically",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58eaa0d0-449d-362e-8dd3-d2ee5b69b323",
                                        "entry_id": "90a5c753-2177-3f20-9c78-f6acb97777bb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To commit (oneself or one's time) solemnly to some aim or task."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "consecrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ebe8954-c2cb-38ad-8b7b-72f3d713e23d",
                                        "entry_id": "dcea39d5-f676-3cd8-802c-a67914ee1e6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Consecrated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc30bc0d-04fb-4042-9827-516173839c99",
                                                "sense_id": "3ebe8954-c2cb-38ad-8b7b-72f3d713e23d",
                                                "text": "Led to the city consecrate to Mars."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "54e5242d-406f-3c75-aab5-542fdbad3e83",
                                        "entry_id": "dcea39d5-f676-3cd8-802c-a67914ee1e6b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Consecrated, devoted, dedicated, sacred."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f788fd3-da2c-48e5-a9a9-2fdd9c757d71",
                                                "sense_id": "54e5242d-406f-3c75-aab5-542fdbad3e83",
                                                "text": "And that this body conſecrate to thee,\nBy Ruffian Luſt ſhould be contaminate!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dde877b0-fd53-4e87-9796-cba279963161",
                                                "sense_id": "54e5242d-406f-3c75-aab5-542fdbad3e83",
                                                "text": "They were assembled in that consecrate place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a606a9da-7808-42b4-9da8-bc09d0d8088d",
                        "source_entry_id": "50715dae-dba3-382a-abb3-22900d3192a0",
                        "source_sense_id": "cfced3b3-64f3-3c5b-a761-48d6047c9f18",
                        "target_lang_word": "ordain",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ordain",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72b859ac-88e2-395f-bece-633907819a69",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To prearrange unalterably."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23b3c4b1-15bf-48b8-999e-f35c1b2b48c4",
                                                "sense_id": "72b859ac-88e2-395f-bece-633907819a69",
                                                "text": "What if the Foot, ordain'd the duſt to tread, / Or Hand, to toil, aſpir'd to be the Head? / What if the Head, the Eye, or Ear repin'd / To ſerve mere Engines to the ruling Mind?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5507163d-a4ae-3f7b-9c7d-ed24711ac7ab",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To decree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e74c719-3f8a-4b43-8190-49c14ce53479",
                                                "sense_id": "5507163d-a4ae-3f7b-9c7d-ed24711ac7ab",
                                                "text": "On once more we swung, bumping uneasily along in the antique narrow-gauge coach, with gloomy woods and gathering night outside, shouts and songs (and quacks) inside—this was not at all the sort of train ordained by the logical strategists in Paris—then grinding to a stop at a mysterious halt which was no more than a nameboard in the pinewoods, without even a footpath leading to it, but nevertheless with a solitary passenger stolidly waiting."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1675e65d-d349-3462-92d2-92ccca371c43",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To admit into the ministry, for example as a priest, bishop, minister or Buddhist monk, or to authorize as a rabbi."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "282b6f75-0ab4-351f-a56e-92e359c80eb4",
                                        "entry_id": "c9486275-53d1-31f5-8c9d-5537924861ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To predestine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
